  "title": "BNCI 2015-004 Mental tasks dataset",
  "description": "EEG recordings from nine end-users with central nervous system tissue damage (stroke or spinal cord injury) performing five cue-guided mental tasks: word association, mental subtraction, spatial navigation, right-hand motor imagery, and feet motor imagery. Data were recorded with 30 active EEG electrodes across two sessions per participant, on different days. The dataset supports brain-computer interface research on individually adapted imagery and binary classification of mental tasks.",
  "methods_description": "30-channel EEG (g.tec g.LADYbird active electrodes, 10-20 montage) was sampled at 256 Hz with 0.5-100 Hz bandpass and 50 Hz notch filtering, plus two EOG channels. Each trial had a 1 s cue followed by 7 s of continuous mental imagery, without feedback. Sessions contained 8 blocks. Manual EOG-based artifact rejection was applied. Classification used LDA on bandpower features with 10-fold cross-validation.",
